{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#782","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#782","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#782\",\"parent_revision\":\"d8bcd68cc6305215c48f12f4cb52861a3150f7fb\",\"root_revision\":\"b2d89664f0b00bb611dfc180feaf9fa1d6f8e26c1f193a8c45f358d96f061bd4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Current state**: The `get_iso_timestamp()` function at line 227 of `task_status_hook.py` calls `datetime.now(UTC).isoformat(timespec=\\\"seconds\\\")` directly. All callers (`handle_subagent_stop`, `handle_post_tool_use`) use this function without the ability to inject a fixed time. Tests for this hook must either mock `datetime.now` at the module level or accept non-deterministic timestamps, making assertions about timestamp ordering or staleness detection fragile.\\n\\nFile: `plugins/python3-development/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py`, line 227-233.\\n\\n**Target state**: `get_iso_timestamp()` accepts an optional `now` parameter (callable returning `datetime`) that defaults to `lambda: datetime.now(UTC)`. Test code passes a fixed `now` callable, enabling deterministic timestamp assertions. The same pattern is applied to any future time-dependent logic (e.g., stall detection threshold comparison).\\n\\n**Measurable signal**: File `task_status_hook.py` contains `def get_iso_timestamp(*, now: Callable[[], datetime] | None = None)`. At least one test in `tests/test_task_status_hook/` calls `get_iso_timestamp(now=lambda: fixed_dt)` and asserts the exact returned string.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-18T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-18T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **deterministic time injection in task_status_hook.py** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/tori-cli.md -- pattern: deterministic time injection for testing\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n5/10 \u2014 Improves test ergonomics for timestamp-dependent assertions; no functional impact on hook behavior. Low urgency, zero risk.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Bottleneck: tests that exercise `handle_activity_update` cannot assert exact `last-activity` timestamps without module-level datetime mocking, which couples tests to the internal import path.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables deterministic timestamp assertions in `handle_activity_update` tests without module-level patching.\\n- Establishes an injectable-time pattern usable in future time-dependent logic (stall detection, threshold comparisons).\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`get_iso_timestamp()` returns an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp string. When called with no arguments, it returns the current time. When called with a `now` callable, it returns the timestamp produced by that callable. Callers passing no `now` argument observe no change in behavior.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n`get_iso_timestamp` accepts an optional keyword-only `now: Callable[[], datetime] | None = None` parameter. When `now` is `None`, it calls `datetime.now(UTC)` as before. `handle_activity_update` at line 698 passes no argument and is unchanged. A test module in `tests/` calls `get_iso_timestamp(now=lambda: fixed_dt)` and asserts the returned string equals `fixed_dt.isoformat(timespec='seconds')`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -n 'def get_iso_timestamp' plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` shows `def get_iso_timestamp(*, now: Callable[[], datetime] | None = None) -> str:`.\\n2. `grep -n 'get_iso_timestamp()' plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` shows the single call-site at line ~698 unchanged (no `now=` argument \u2014 uses the default).\\n3. A test exists in `tests/` that calls `hook.get_iso_timestamp(now=lambda: fixed_dt)` and asserts `== fixed_dt.isoformat(timespec='seconds')`.\\n4. `uv run pytest tests/test_task_status_hook_profiles.py -x` exits 0.\\n5. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` exits 0.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` lines 356\u2013362 (definition), 698 (sole caller inside `handle_activity_update`) |\\n| Existing tests | `/home/user/claude_skills/tests/test_task_status_hook_profiles.py` \u2014 shows test fixture and import patterns to follow |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 one function signature change (2 lines), one new test (~10 lines). No callers need updating: `handle_activity_update` calls `get_iso_timestamp()` with no arguments and is unaffected by the new optional parameter.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 all information is available. Description contained stale metadata (line 227 \u2192 actual line 356; path `plugins/python3-development/...` \u2192 actual `plugins/development-harness/...`). Verified against source.\\n\",\"digest\":\"c74a625f9c9a937a2b70a452032845bb8af8b2e3e9f3d615bf2a50472f1e7093\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgytag\"}"}